01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:06,000
The Music Lovers is a 1971 British drama film directed by Ken Russell
and starring Richard Chamberlain and Glenda Jackson.

11
01:30:12,000 --> 01:30:18,000
The screenplay by Melvyn Bragg, based on Beloved Friend, a collection of personal correspondence edited by Catherine Drinker Bowen
and Barbara von Meck, focuses on the life and career of 19th-century Russian composer Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky.

12
01:38:24,000 --> 01:38:30,000
It was one of the director's biographical films about classical composers, which include Elgar (1962), Delius: Song
of Summer (1968), Mahler (1974) and Lisztomania (1975), made from an often idiosyncratic standpoint.

13
01:46:36,000 --> 01:46:42,000
The film explores themes of composer, biography, historical
figure, male homosexuality, 19th century.

14
01:54:48,000 --> 01:54:54,000
The tone is emotional.
